  "body": "It's one of the -webkit- prefixes supported by Edge, and a number of high priority mobile sites depend on it ([goog calendar](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=995140) and gmail being two).\n\nAccording to Chrome platform status, usage currently hovers right around 1% of page loads:\nhttps://www.chromestatus.com/metrics/css/timeline/popularity/196\n\nhttp://dbaron.org/log/20120612-border-image is a good resource for why this _can't_ be a simple alias to unprefixed border-image.\n\nHere's a simple test page with some code from google calendar: http://jsbin.com/gafinudopa/4/edit?html,css,output.\n\nBoth Chrome and Edge have the same output.\n\n@jacobrossi - is there someone who worked on `-webkit-border-image` who would be willing to share notes on how y'all implemented it?\n",
